    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d603">

                <pb facs="0913" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.79611 Pan American Airways, Inc./86:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gross</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-06-29T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1928—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 2:45 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. Department’s 33, June 28, 1 p.m.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d603-f1"/> Haitian
                    Government authorizes ship of the Pan American Airways to make contemplated
                    flight. Permission also granted to use local Marine Corps’ landing field for
                    this flight. The question of the Government granting permission for
                    establishment of a regular service by this company will be considered but
                    anticipate no difficulty in this regard. See my despatch No. 1050, August 8,
                    1927, High Commissioner’s Series.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d603-f2"/> Please
                    request pilot to telegraph ahead day and hour of arrival here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gross</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
